{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2157-12-24 23:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during this stay. You came in with abdominal pain and high blood sugar. Can you tell me more about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2157-12-24 23:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi. Yeah, the pain in my upper belly is back—same as always. It’s from my gastroparesis or pancreatitis, I think. I’ve been vomiting at home, but not since I got here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2157-12-24 23:43:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. Your blood sugar was very high—615—when you arrived. But your labs don’t show ketoacidosis. We gave you insulin and fluids in the ER. How have you been feeling since then?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2157-12-24 23:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. The pain’s still there, but not as bad. I got some Dilaudid in the ER. That helped."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2157-12-24 23:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep managing your pain with oral Dilaudid, as per your usual plan. No IV narcotics, since your primary doctor has set limits. We’ll also monitor your blood sugar closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2157-12-24 23:49:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s fine. I know the rules. But can I eat? I’m kind of hungry."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2157-12-24 23:51:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start you on clear liquids and see how you do. If you tolerate it, we can advance your diet. But avoid greasy or sugary foods—they can make your symptoms worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2157-12-25 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs from last night were mostly stable. Lipase was normal, which is reassuring—no sign of acute pancreatitis flare. Blood sugar this morning is 269."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2157-12-25 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s still high, right? My Lantus dose at home is 70 units, but I only took 40 last night because I wasn’t eating much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2157-12-25 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re giving you 50 units of Lantus at night while you’re here, plus a tighter sliding scale. We suspect you’re eating more regularly in the hospital, so we’ll adjust accordingly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2157-12-25 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. But I’ve been trying to stick to my routine. My port-a-cath is working fine for insulin, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2157-12-25 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your port is intact and we’re using it for meds. We’ll keep monitoring your sugars and adjust as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2157-12-25 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I noticed you had some pizza brought in. How did that sit with you?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2157-12-25 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I felt okay after. No vomiting. But my belly was a little more sore."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2157-12-25 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’d recommend avoiding fried or fatty foods. They can worsen both gastroparesis and pancreatitis. Stick to lighter meals when possible."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2157-12-25 14:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll try. But it’s hard when visitors bring food."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2157-12-25 20:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did a bladder scan, and it showed over 600 cc—quite full. You’re having trouble urinating?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2157-12-25 20:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, I’ve had this before. Urinary retention. It comes and goes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2157-12-25 20:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll need to straight catheterize you to empty your bladder. This could be from the narcotics, diphenhydramine, or just not moving around much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2157-12-25 20:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Again? I hate that. But okay, if I have to."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2157-12-26 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your urine culture came back—just normal flora, no infection. We’ll keep monitoring your bladder. You may need a Foley if retention continues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2157-12-26 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I have to go home with a catheter?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2157-12-26 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not if we can help it. We’re hoping to get you voiding on your own. We’ll try removing the Foley later if things improve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2157-12-26 13:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Doctor, can I talk to someone? My roommate’s been hitting me. I’m scared to go back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2157-12-26 13:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m so sorry to hear that. I’ll get the social worker and domestic violence team to speak with you right away. You’re safe here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2157-12-26 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The social worker met with you. They’ll help you file a restraining order and find safer housing if needed. Is there anything else you’re worried about?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2157-12-26 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just getting my pain under control. And not going low on insulin. I had a bad low last week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2157-12-26 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re checking your sugars regularly. You’ve had a few lows, so we adjusted your sliding scale. We’re keeping your Lantus at 50 units for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2157-12-27 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood sugar has been more stable. We’re increasing your Lantus to 60 units tonight to better match your needs. How’s the pain today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2157-12-27 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still there, but I’m managing with the oral Dilaudid. I haven’t needed more than every 3 hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2157-12-27 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. And you’ve been eating without vomiting. That’s progress. We’ll keep working on getting your bladder function back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2157-12-27 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We removed the straight catheter. You were able to void about 400 cc. That’s a good sign. We’ll keep doing scans to make sure you’re emptying well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2157-12-27 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad. I don’t want to leave with a Foley."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2157-12-27 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll avoid it if possible. But if retention returns, we may need it temporarily. We also scheduled a urology follow-up for you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2157-12-28 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve had two successful voids with post-void residuals under 100 cc. That’s excellent. We won’t need a Foley."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2157-12-28 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. That’s a relief."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2157-12-28 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your sugars are still fluctuating, but overall better. We’ll send you home on 60 units of Lantus at bedtime and your usual sliding scale."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2157-12-28 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my pain meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2157-12-28 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Same as before—Dilaudid 2 mg every 3 hours as needed. We’re giving you 20 tablets. No refills, per your contract."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2157-12-28 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I understand. I’ll stick to the plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2157-12-29 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Today’s the day we’re planning to discharge you. You’re tolerating food, pain is stable, sugars are improving, and you’re urinating on your own."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2157-12-29 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. What about my anxiety? I’ve been using my Valium."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2157-12-29 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You can continue diazepam as needed—two 5 mg tablets every 8 hours. We’ve also adjusted some of your sleep meds to lower doses to reduce side effects."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2157-12-29 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my G-tube? It’s just for meds, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2157-12-29 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s in good condition. You’ll continue using it for medications as before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2157-12-29 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2157-12-29 10:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll see your primary doctor this week. We’ve also set up an appointment with urology for your bladder issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2157-12-30 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set for discharge. Avoid fatty or sugary foods, take your meds as prescribed, and call your doctor if you have worsening pain, vomiting, or trouble urinating."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2157-12-30 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I’m going to file that restraining order. Thanks for listening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2157-12-30 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care of yourself. We’re here if you need us."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2157-12-30 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One more thing—my sugars were high when I came in. Was that dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2157-12-30 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, 615 is very high, but you didn’t have ketoacidosis. Still, it’s important to manage it closely. That’s why we increased your Lantus dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2157-12-30 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll keep checking my sugars."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2157-12-30 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good plan. And remember, if you feel confused, dizzy, or shaky, check it right away—it could be low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2157-12-30 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know. I’ve had lows before. I always carry juice."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2157-12-30 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. That’s exactly what to do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2157-12-30 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my asthma? I haven’t used my inhalers much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2157-12-30 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your lungs sounded clear. Keep using your fluticasone-salmeterol twice daily, and albuterol if you feel tight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2157-12-30 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2157-12-30 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Alright, the discharge papers are ready. A nurse will go over everything with you one more time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2157-12-30 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee. I feel better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2157-12-30 08:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m glad. Take care and stay safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2157-12-30 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2157-12-30 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll see you in follow-up. Call if anything changes before then."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2157-12-30 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2157-12-30 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2157-12-30 08:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2157-12-24 23:39:00",
    "admission_end": "2157-12-30 13:15:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted with acute-on-chronic epigastric abdominal pain, attributed to gastroparesis and chronic pancreatitis, along with severe hyperglycemia (glucose 615) without ketoacidosis. Pain was managed with oral hydromorphone per her narcotic contract, and insulin therapy was adjusted from 50 to 60 units of Lantus nightly due to improved oral intake and fluctuating glucose levels. She developed urinary retention likely due to narcotics and sedatives, requiring intermittent catheterization; however, she regained spontaneous voiding and did not require a Foley at discharge. A domestic violence concern was addressed, with plans for a restraining order and social support. She remained on her baseline psychiatric and gastrointestinal medications, with no major complications. She was discharged home in stable condition with follow-up arranged with her primary care provider and urology.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Acute pancreatitis",
      "Chronic pancreatitis",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Other specified retention of urine",
      "Borderline personality disorder",
      "Abdominal pain, epigastric"
    ]
  }
}
